-- program.lth: the rules of the checker as the laws of `WellFormed`.
--
-- Draft 0, 2026-10-13, by Claude Opus 5.5 in the session (step 3.1 of
-- record/plan-from-zero-2026-10-13-execution.md). Sources: spec 4, its rules 4.R1 to 4.R13 and the
-- statements 4.S14, 4.S17, 4.S21, 4.S23, 4.S24; spec 1.S7 (D(n), B(n)); spec 5.S9, 5.S10
-- (`Failures E`); L2.7, L14. The pattern is that of ebnf.lth and term.lth.
--
-- What this file states (4.S21). A model of `WellFormed` is a checker: from a program it gives the
-- failures it finds. Each rule of chapter 4 is a predicate, `violates`, written here as the rule
-- says it, and two generic laws, `ReportsViolations` and `ReportsNoFalseFailure`, say the checker reports a failure of that rule
-- for a name exactly when the name violates it. So the rule is stated once, as a predicate, and
-- the checker is held to it; the accept and reject programs of `tests/spec/` are its cases. The
-- Python checker (step 4) is a specimen.
--
-- Which program. The rules read what is written: whether an alias is written with `=` (4.R7),
-- `:=` against `<-` (4.R12), a body that is an `extern` (4.R5). So `WellFormed` takes the surface
-- program of grammar.lth; the rules that need the type of a term (4.R8, 4.R9, 4.R11, 4.R13) read
-- it through a typing, a theory of its own (§4), over the elaborated `Term` of term.lth.
--
-- Index. Status of each section: done, or todo with what it needs. A session or Codex continuing
-- this file takes the first todo, writes it in the pattern of the done ones, checks it with
-- `luthier parse src/luthier/lib/program.lth`, sets its status to done here, and commits.
--
--   §1 Failures and the theory: `Failure`, `Report`, `Elaboration` (translation.lth),
--      `WellFormed` over an alpha, a substitution, an elaboration
--      and a typing, the generic laws `ReportsViolations`, `ReportsNoFalseFailure` (4.S21, 5.S9). done
--   §2 Names: the acts' names, D(n) and B(n) on the surface tree (1.S7). Type and
--      term position (4.S2) still to add, for 4.R2.                                 done
--   §3 The rules that read names and forms: 4.R1, 4.R2 (existence), 4.R3 with L2.7,
--      4.R4, 4.R5, 4.R7, 4.R12 (top level), 4.S14. Still to add: 4.R2 by position and
--      theory, 4.R12 inside blocks.                                                 done
--   §4 Typing: variables, constants, lambda and application, the universe; refinement
--      with variance (4.R9); the branch of a condition (4.R11).                       done
--   §5 The rules that read types: 4.R6, 4.R8, 4.R9. 4.R11 is a law of the typing;
--      4.R13 and 4.S23 are laws of the elaboration (step 2.4).                        done
--   §6 Reports: provisional externs, loose functions (4.S17); 4.R10 and 4.S20 by name
--      only, the author's judgement.                                                  done
--   §7 `WellFormed :=` the conjunction.                                               done

import "grammar.lth" SurfaceProgram SurfaceAct Surface SurfacePattern LambdaParam Item Field Binder Body
  Clause ImportName declare define alias importAct operatorAct datum explicit implicit termBody dataBody
  clausesBody name literal universe world app binop neg tuple pi sigma sigmaNamed record
  subtype recordValue block sum list lambda matchOf namedArg ifThen proj quoted pWild pApp pLit pTuple
  plainParam typedParam shapeParam bind rebind
import "term.lth" Term Program Act Constant Pattern Alpha AlphaPair Substitution Var Lit Universe World Lam App Pi
  Sigma Pair Match Inj Sum Data Subtype Extern Primitive Axiom Hole Record RecordValue Proj Let Declare Define Datum IntConst FloatConst
  StringConst PCon

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §1 Failures and the theory

-- A failure names its rule, the name it is about, and says why (5.S9: a check is written in the
-- form that explains its failures). `Failures E` of 5.S9 is the list of them; its projections are
-- checks.lth's (5.S10, step 3.3).
Failure = { rule : String, name : String, message : String }

-- The elaboration of a surface program into the kernel's `Program` (2.S12, 3.S30) is
-- translation.lth's theory; the rules on types read what a definition elaborates to.
import "translation.lth" Elaboration

-- A checker, held to an elaboration and a typing (§4): the failures it finds in a program
-- (4.S21), and what it reports without rejecting (4.S19, §6).
Report = { kind : String, name : String, message : String }
WellFormed (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) : {
  check : SurfaceProgram -> List Failure,
  report : SurfaceProgram -> List Report,
}

member (x : String) (xs : List String) : Bool := match xs { nil -> false ; cons y rest -> x == y or member x rest }
concat (xs ys : List String) : List String := match xs { nil -> ys ; cons x rest -> cons x (concat rest ys) }
remove (x : String) (xs : List String) : List String :=
  match xs { nil -> nil ; cons y rest -> if x == y then remove x rest else cons y (remove x rest) }
removeAll (xs ys : List String) : List String := match xs { nil -> ys ; cons x rest -> removeAll rest (remove x ys) }

reported (fs : List Failure) (rule n : String) : Bool :=
  match fs { nil -> false ; cons f rest -> (f.rule == rule and f.name == n) or reported rest rule n }

-- The programs a rule is tested on, and its two laws (review of layers 0-1, B). A law stated over
-- every program with one of its names would be vacuous in practice: a random program violates
-- some rules almost always and others almost never, so only one side of "exactly" would be seen
-- (L9.6). So each rule has two domains, the programs with a name that violates it and those with
-- a name that does not, and two laws. Their generators are the certifier's (7.R1): the accept and
-- reject programs of tests/spec/ as a census, and well-formed programs drawn from a small pool of
-- names and changed by one edit aimed at the rule. A predicate that states only part of its rule
-- (4.R2, 4.R12 at the top level, the rules on types until `Typing` is complete) under-approximates
-- the violations, so only its sound direction, "violates implies reported", is a law: "exactly"
-- would fail a checker that implements the whole rule.
Violating (violates : SurfaceProgram -> String -> Bool) : U :=
  { p : SurfaceProgram, n : String | member n (actNames p) and violates p n }
Clean (violates : SurfaceProgram -> String -> Bool) : U :=
  { p : SurfaceProgram, n : String | member n (actNames p) and not (violates p n) }
ReportsViolations (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (rule : String)
                  (violates : SurfaceProgram -> String -> Bool) (w : WellFormed a sb e t) (c : Violating violates) : Bool :=
  reported (w.check c.p) rule c.n
ReportsNoFalseFailure (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (rule : String)
                      (violates : SurfaceProgram -> String -> Bool) (w : WellFormed a sb e t) (c : Clean violates) : Bool :=
  not (reported (w.check c.p) rule c.n)
-- and it reports nothing about names the program does not introduce
ReportsOnItsNames (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (w : WellFormed a sb e t)
                  (p : SurfaceProgram) : Bool := failuresNamed (w.check p) (actNames p)
failuresNamed (fs : List Failure) (ns : List String) : Bool :=
  match fs { nil -> true ; cons f rest -> member f.name ns and failuresNamed rest ns }

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §2 Names

-- the name an act introduces, if any, and the names of a program
actName (a : SurfaceAct) : Maybe String := match a {
  declare x bs t -> just x ; define x bs t b -> just x ; alias x bs t -> just x ;
  importAct f ns -> nothing ; operatorAct o t -> nothing ; datum t -> nothing ;
}
actNames (p : SurfaceProgram) : List String :=
  match p { nil -> nil ; cons a rest -> match actName a { nothing -> actNames rest ; just x -> cons x (actNames rest) } }
importedNames (p : SurfaceProgram) : List String := match p { nil -> nil ;
  cons a rest -> match a { importAct f ns -> concat (importNames ns) (importedNames rest) ; _ -> importedNames rest } }
importNames (ns : List ImportName) : List String := match ns { nil -> nil ;
  cons i rest -> cons (match i.asName { nothing -> i.name ; just y -> y }) (importNames rest) }

isDeclared (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  match p { nil -> false ; cons a rest -> match a { declare x bs t -> x == n or isDeclared rest n ; _ -> isDeclared rest n } }
isDefined (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  match p { nil -> false ; cons a rest -> match a { define x bs t b -> x == n or isDefined rest n ; _ -> isDefined rest n } }
isAlias (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  match p { nil -> false ; cons a rest -> match a { alias x bs t -> x == n or isAlias rest n ; _ -> isAlias rest n } }
-- a name is known when the program introduces it, imports it, makes it a constructor, or core
-- gives it (`core` the list of core's names: core is not written yet, 12.S21). A dotted name
-- `m.f` is known when the whole name is, or its first part (2.S14: a qualified name, or a
-- projection of a variable or definition); `namePrefix` gives the part before the first `.`, and
-- the name itself when it has none (a function of core's `String`, 11, declared here until core
-- names it; review of layers 0-1, B).
namePrefix : String -> String
known (core : List String) (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  knownWhole core p n or knownWhole core p (namePrefix n)
knownWhole (core : List String) (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  member n (actNames p) or member n (importedNames p) or member n (constructors p) or member n core

-- The constructors of the `data` of a program: a pattern `name` is one of them if it names one,
-- and a variable otherwise (2.S10, 2.S13).
constructors (p : SurfaceProgram) : List String := match p { nil -> nil ;
  cons a rest -> match a { define x bs t b -> concat (bodyConstructors b) (constructors rest) ; _ -> constructors rest } }
bodyConstructors (b : Body) : List String := match b { dataBody cs -> pairNames cs ; _ -> nil }
pairNames (kvs : List (String * Surface)) : List String := match kvs { nil -> nil ; cons (k, v) rest -> cons k (pairNames rest) }

-- the variables a pattern binds, given the constructors `k`
patternBinds (k : List String) (q : SurfacePattern) : List String := match q {
  pWild -> nil ; pLit l -> nil ;
  pApp n qs -> if member n k then patternsBind k qs else (match qs { nil -> [n] ; _ -> patternsBind k qs }) ;
  pTuple qs -> patternsBind k qs ;
}
patternsBind (k : List String) (qs : List SurfacePattern) : List String :=
  match qs { nil -> nil ; cons q rest -> concat (patternBinds k q) (patternsBind k rest) }

-- spec 1.S7: the names found in a term, less those it binds; operators are core's and not counted
namesIn (k : List String) (t : Surface) : List String := match t {
  name s -> [s] ;
  literal l -> nil ; universe -> nil ; world -> nil ;
  app f a -> concat (namesIn k f) (namesIn k a) ;
  binop o a b -> concat (namesIn k a) (namesIn k b) ;
  neg a -> namesIn k a ; quoted a -> namesIn k a ; namedArg x a -> namesIn k a ; proj a x -> namesIn k a ;
  tuple ts -> namesInAll k ts ; list ts -> namesInAll k ts ;
  pi xs a b -> concat (namesIn k a) (removeAll xs (namesIn k b)) ;
  sigma xs a b -> concat (namesIn k a) (removeAll xs (namesIn k b)) ;
  sigmaNamed x a y b -> concat (namesIn k a) (remove x (namesIn k b)) ;
  record fs law -> concat (fieldsNames k fs) (match law { nothing -> nil ; just l -> removeAll (fieldLabels fs) (namesIn k l) }) ;
  subtype q a law -> concat (namesIn k a) (removeAll (patternBinds k q) (namesIn k law)) ;
  recordValue kvs -> pairsNames k kvs ; sum kvs -> pairsNames k kvs ;
  block items e -> itemsNames k items e ;
  lambda ps items e -> concat (paramsNames k ps) (removeAll (paramsBind k ps) (itemsNames k items e)) ;
  matchOf s arms -> concat (namesIn k s) (armsNames k arms) ;
  ifThen c a b -> concat (namesIn k c) (concat (namesIn k a) (match b { nothing -> nil ; just e -> namesIn k e })) ;
}
namesInAll (k : List String) (ts : List Surface) : List String :=
  match ts { nil -> nil ; cons t rest -> concat (namesIn k t) (namesInAll k rest) }
pairsNames (k : List String) (kvs : List (String * Surface)) : List String :=
  match kvs { nil -> nil ; cons (x, v) rest -> concat (namesIn k v) (pairsNames k rest) }
fieldLabels (fs : List Field) : List String := match fs { nil -> nil ; cons f rest -> concat f.names (fieldLabels rest) }
-- a field's names are in scope in the fields after it (a dependent record, 2.S14)
fieldsNames (k : List String) (fs : List Field) : List String :=
  match fs { nil -> nil ; cons f rest -> concat (namesIn k f.type) (removeAll f.names (fieldsNames k rest)) }
-- a block's items bind in what follows them
itemsNames (k : List String) (items : List Item) (e : Surface) : List String := match items {
  nil -> namesIn k e ;
  cons it rest -> match it {
    bind x t -> concat (namesIn k t) (remove x (itemsNames k rest e)) ;
    rebind x t -> concat (namesIn k t) (remove x (itemsNames k rest e)) } }
paramsBind (k : List String) (ps : List LambdaParam) : List String := match ps { nil -> nil ;
  cons q rest -> concat (match q { plainParam x -> [x] ; typedParam xs t -> xs ; shapeParam qs -> patternsBind k qs })
                        (paramsBind k rest) }
-- a parameter's names are in scope in the parameters after it
paramsNames (k : List String) (ps : List LambdaParam) : List String := match ps { nil -> nil ;
  cons q rest -> concat (match q { typedParam xs t -> namesIn k t ; _ -> nil }) (removeAll (paramsBind k [q]) (paramsNames k rest)) }
armsNames (k : List String) (arms : List (SurfacePattern * Surface)) : List String := match arms { nil -> nil ;
  cons (q, b) rest -> concat (removeAll (patternBinds k q) (namesIn k b)) (armsNames k rest) }

-- D(n) and B(n) of 1.S7: the names in the declared type of `n` (its binders included) and in its
-- body, each less the binders' own names
-- a binder's names are in scope in the binders after it: `(a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a)`, a
-- default mentioning an earlier parameter, `{A : U} (x : A)` (2.S7, 2.S16)
binderNames (k : List String) (bs : List Binder) : List String := match bs { nil -> nil ;
  cons b rest -> concat (match b { explicit xs t d -> concat (namesIn k t) (match d { nothing -> nil ; just e -> namesIn k e }) ;
                                   implicit xs t -> namesIn k t })
                        (removeAll (binderBound [b]) (binderNames k rest)) }
binderBound (bs : List Binder) : List String := match bs { nil -> nil ;
  cons b rest -> concat (match b { explicit xs t d -> xs ; implicit xs t -> xs }) (binderBound rest) }
bodyNames (k : List String) (b : Body) : List String := match b {
  termBody t -> namesIn k t ;
  dataBody cs -> pairsNames k cs ;
  clausesBody cs -> clausesNames k cs ;
}
clausesNames (k : List String) (cs : List Clause) : List String := match cs { nil -> nil ;
  cons c rest -> concat (removeAll (patternsBind k c.patterns) (namesIn k c.body)) (clausesNames k rest) }
dOf (p : SurfaceProgram) (a : SurfaceAct) : List String := match a {
  declare x bs t -> concat (binderNames (constructors p) bs) (removeAll (binderBound bs) (namesIn (constructors p) t)) ;
  define x bs t b -> concat (binderNames (constructors p) bs)
                            (match t { nothing -> nil ; just u -> removeAll (binderBound bs) (namesIn (constructors p) u) }) ;
  alias x bs t -> concat (binderNames (constructors p) bs) (removeAll (binderBound bs) (namesIn (constructors p) t)) ;
  _ -> nil ;
}
bOf (p : SurfaceProgram) (a : SurfaceAct) : List String := match a {
  define x bs t b -> removeAll (binderBound bs) (bodyNames (constructors p) b) ;
  _ -> nil ;
}

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §3 The rules that read names and forms

-- core's names: core encloses every file (12.S21) and is not written yet, so its names are a hole
coreNames : List String

actsNamed (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : List SurfaceAct := match p { nil -> nil ;
  cons a rest -> match actName a { just x -> if x == n then cons a (actsNamed rest n) else actsNamed rest n ;
                                   nothing -> actsNamed rest n } }
anyUnknown (p : SurfaceProgram) (ms : List String) : Bool :=
  match ms { nil -> false ; cons m rest -> not (known coreNames p m) or anyUnknown p rest }
anyAct (f : SurfaceAct -> Bool) (acts : List SurfaceAct) : Bool :=
  match acts { nil -> false ; cons a rest -> f a or anyAct f rest }
count (n : String) (xs : List String) : Nat := match xs { nil -> 0 ; cons x rest -> (if x == n then 1 else 0) + count n rest }
definedNames (p : SurfaceProgram) : List String :=
  match p { nil -> nil ; cons a rest -> match a { define x bs t b -> cons x (definedNames rest) ; _ -> definedNames rest } }

-- 4.R1: a declaration mentions only names that exist, declared or defined (or imported, or core's)
violatesR1 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  anyAct (fn a { match a { declare x bs t -> anyUnknown p (dOf p a) ; _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)

-- 4.R2, the part that reads names: the names a definition mentions exist. That a name in type
-- position is defined unless it is in the definition's own theory needs type position (4.S2) and
-- the theories (4.S3, the strongly connected components): todo, §2.
violatesR2Exists (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  anyAct (fn a { match a { define x bs t b -> anyUnknown p (concat (dOf p a) (bOf p a)) ; _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)

-- 4.R3: a predicate touches what it is over: every label of a record with a law, the variables of
-- a subtype's pattern; and (L2.7, D-2026-10-13-p) every constructor of a `data` is mentioned by
-- some law. A law is read here as a definition whose declared type is `Bool`, until typing (§4)
-- can say which definitions are laws; whether the law states the constructor's role, and not
-- only lists it, a test cannot decide (4.S19 reports it).
untouched (k : List String) (labels : List String) (law : Surface) : Bool :=
  match labels { nil -> false ; cons l rest -> not (member l (namesIn k law)) or untouched k rest law }
predicateUntouched (k : List String) (t : Surface) : Bool := match t {
  record fs law -> match law { nothing -> false ; just l -> untouched k (fieldLabels fs) l } ;
  subtype q a law -> untouched k (patternBinds k q) law ;
  _ -> false ;
}
lawNames (p : SurfaceProgram) : List String := match p { nil -> nil ; cons a rest -> match a {
  define x bs t b -> (match t { just (name "Bool") -> concat (bOf p a) (lawNames rest) ; _ -> lawNames rest }) ;
  _ -> lawNames rest } }
anyUnclaimed (p : SurfaceProgram) (cs : List String) : Bool :=
  match cs { nil -> false ; cons c rest -> not (member c (lawNames p)) or anyUnclaimed p rest }
violatesR3 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  anyAct (fn a { match a {
    define x bs t b -> (match b { termBody u -> predicateUntouched (constructors p) u ;
                                  dataBody cs -> anyUnclaimed p (pairNames cs) ; _ -> false }) ;
    _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)

-- the declared type of a name: the one its definition writes, or its declaration's when the
-- definition writes none (`P : U` then `P := ...`; review of layers 0-1, B)
typeOfAct (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) (t : Maybe Surface) : Maybe Surface :=
  match t { just u -> just u ; nothing -> declaredSurface p n }
declaredSurface (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Maybe Surface := match p { nil -> nothing ;
  cons act rest -> match act { declare x bs t -> if x == n then just t else declaredSurface rest n ; _ -> declaredSurface rest n } }
atUniverse (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) (t : Maybe Surface) : Bool := typeOfAct p n t == just universe

-- 4.R4: a definition at `U` makes a new type only if its body is a subtype with a predicate, a
-- record with a law, or a `data` (a whitelist, as the rule reads); any other body at `U`, an
-- anonymous structure or a type already named, is to be an alias. An extern is 4.R5's.
makesAType (b : Body) : Bool := match b {
  dataBody cs -> true ;
  termBody u -> (match u { subtype q a law -> true ; record fs law -> not (law == nothing) ; _ -> isExtern u }) ;
  clausesBody cs -> false ;
}
violatesR4 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  anyAct (fn act { match act { define x bs t b -> atUniverse p n t and not (makesAType b) ; _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)

-- 4.R5: an extern gives a value, never a type, unless it is provisional
isExtern (t : Surface) : Bool := match t { app f a -> isExtern f ; name s -> s == "extern" ; _ -> false }
isProvisional (t : Surface) : Bool :=
  match t { app f a -> (match a { namedArg x v -> x == "provisional" ; _ -> false }) or isProvisional f ; _ -> false }
-- and its type must be defined (4.R2 applies to an extern as to any body)
violatesR5 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  anyAct (fn act { match act { define x bs t b ->
    (match b { termBody u -> isExtern u and not (isProvisional u) ; _ -> false })
    and (atUniverse p n t or (match typeOfAct p n t { just (name m) -> not (isDefined p m) and not (member m coreNames) ;
                                                        _ -> false })) ;
    _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)

-- 4.R7: an alias is neither declared nor defined
violatesR7 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool := isAlias p n and (isDeclared p n or isDefined p n)

-- 4.R12 at the top level: `:=` defines once (a `<-` there does not parse, 2.R5). Inside blocks,
-- `:=` of a name already bound and `<-` of a name bound with `:=`: todo, a walk of the bodies.
violatesR12 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool := count n (definedNames p) >= 2

-- 4.S14: a law no type claims defines nothing; it is a branch, and 4.R2 applies to it, so it is
-- reported, not rejected (§6; review of layers 0-1, B). Read, as in 4.R3, as a definition at
-- `Bool` that no other definition's body mentions.
otherBodies (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : List String := match p { nil -> nil ; cons a rest -> match a {
  define x bs t b -> if x == n then otherBodies rest n else concat (bOf p a) (otherBodies rest n) ;
  _ -> otherBodies rest n } }
violatesS14 (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  anyAct (fn a { match a { define x bs t b -> t == just (name "Bool") and not (member n (otherBodies p n)) ; _ -> false } })
         (actsNamed p n)

-- 4.S17, no loose functions, rejects only once local definitions exist; until then it is a report
-- (§6), and the theory files themselves hold such helpers, as 12.S23 allows.


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §4 Typing

-- The type of an elaborated term in a program and a context of typed variables, if it has one;
-- `same`, the definitional equality of types (3.S20); `refines`, that a value of the first type
-- passes where the second is expected (3.S6, 4.R9); `branchContext`, the context inside the
-- `true` or `false` branch of a condition (4.R11). Only what the rules of §5 need is stated; the
-- type formers of 3 §2 get their roles here, as the computing constructors got theirs from
-- `Reduction` (term.lth).
Context = List (String * Term)
Typing (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) : {
  typeOf : Program -> Context -> Term -> Maybe Term,
  same : Term -> Term -> Bool,
  refines : Term -> Term -> Bool,
  branchContext : Context -> Term -> Bool -> Context,
}

typed (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (r : Maybe Term) (ty : Term) : Bool :=
  match r { nothing -> false ; just u -> t.same u ty }
lookup (x : String) (ctx : Context) : Maybe Term :=
  match ctx { nil -> nothing ; cons (y, ty) rest -> if x == y then just ty else lookup x rest }

-- a variable has the type its context gives it; a constant the type of its kind (spec 11)
-- (Laws stated on terms that type by construction, not as implications whose premise a random
-- term rarely meets; and `same` and `refines` held apart from the trivial relations, which made
-- every law hold before; review of layers 0-1, B.)
int : Term := Var "Int"
lit (i : Int) : Term := Lit (IntConst i)

-- a variable has the type its context gives it, a global name the type its declaration gives it
-- (a definition's type, `Define` carrying it, likewise); a constant the type of its kind (spec 11)
TypeOfVar (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (x : String) (ty : Term) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p (cons (x, ty) ctx) (Var x)) ty
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf [Declare x ty] [] (Var x)) ty
TypeOfConstant (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (i : Int) (u : Float64) (s : String) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (lit i)) int and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Lit (FloatConst u))) (Var "Float64")
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Lit (StringConst s))) (Var "String")
-- the exponential: a lambda has the dependent function type of its body, applied to an argument
-- of its domain the type of its body with the argument for the variable (3 §2, 3.S5); an
-- application of what is not a function has no type
TypeOfLam (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (x : String) (ty : Term) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Lam x ty (Var x))) (Pi x ty ty)
TypeOfApp (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (x : String) (i : Int) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (App (Lam x int (Var x)) (lit i))) int
  and t.typeOf p ctx (App (lit i) (lit i)) == nothing
-- the product, the record and its projection, the sum's injection, a match's arm (3 §2)
TypeOfIntroductions (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (i j : Int) (x y : String) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Pair (lit i) (lit j))) (Sigma "_" int int)
  and (x == y or (typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (RecordValue [(x, lit i), (y, lit j)])) (Record [(x, int), (y, int)])
                  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Proj (RecordValue [(x, lit i), (y, lit j)]) y)) int))
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Match (lit i) [(PWild, lit j)])) int
-- the type formers are types: their role (L2.7) is to form types, of type `U` when their parts are
TypeOfFormers (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (x l : String) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Pi x int int)) Universe and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Sigma x int int)) Universe
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Sum [(l, int)])) Universe and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Record [(l, int)])) Universe
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Subtype x int (Var "true"))) Universe
  and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Data x [(l, Var x)])) Universe
-- a local definition is transparent: inside it the name is the value (D-2026-10-13-aa, Q1)
TypeOfLet (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) (x : String) (i : Int) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx (Let x int (lit i) (Var x))) int
-- the universe is a type, and the world (D-2026-10-13-b); version 0 keeps `U : U` (3.S8)
TypeOfUniverse (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : Program) (ctx : Context) : Bool :=
  typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx Universe) Universe and typed a sb t (t.typeOf p ctx World) Universe

-- `same`, definitional equality of types (3.S20): alpha-equal types are the same, a defined type
-- name is its body, and distinct heads are not the same
SameIsAlpha (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (q : AlphaPair a) : Bool := t.same q.s q.t
SameSeparates (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) : Bool :=
  not (t.same Universe int) and not (t.same int (Var "String")) and not (t.same int (Pi "_" int int))

-- refinement: reflexive; a subtype refines its base (3.S6); functions contravariant in the
-- domain and covariant in the codomain (4.R9), over pairs it relates; distinct bases do not refine
-- one another, and a base does not refine a subtype of it
RefinePair (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) : U := { small big : Term | t.refines small big }
RefinesItself (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ty : Term) : Bool := t.refines ty ty
SubtypeRefinesBase (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (x : String) (ty q : Term) : Bool :=
  t.refines (Subtype x ty q) ty
RefinesFunctions (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (x : String) (d c : RefinePair a sb t) : Bool :=
  t.refines (Pi x d.big c.small) (Pi x d.small c.big)
RefinesSeparates (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (x : String) : Bool :=
  not (t.refines (Var "String") int) and not (t.refines int (Subtype x int (App (App (Var "<") (lit 0)) (Var x))))

-- 4.R11: inside the branch of a condition `c` in which a variable `x : T` occurs, `x` has the
-- subtype `{ x : T | c }`, and inside the other `{ x : T | not c }`; the same holds of a pattern:
-- in the arm `just y`, the scrutinee is `just y` (stated by the arm's context, as the variable's)
branchesRefine (ctx : Context) (t : Context -> Term -> Bool -> Context) (x : String) (c ty : Term) : Bool :=
  lookup x (t (cons (x, ty) ctx) c true) == just (Subtype x ty c)
  and lookup x (t (cons (x, ty) ctx) c false) == just (Subtype x ty (App (Var "not") c))
-- stated on two conditions in which `x` occurs: a predicate applied to it, and `0 < x`
BranchRefines (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ctx : Context) (x q : String) (ty : Term) : Bool :=
  branchesRefine ctx t.branchContext x (App (Var q) (Var x)) ty
  and branchesRefine ctx t.branchContext x (App (App (Var "<") (lit 0)) (Var x)) ty

Typing (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) := TypeOfVar a sb & TypeOfConstant a sb & TypeOfLam a sb & TypeOfApp a sb
  & TypeOfIntroductions a sb & TypeOfFormers a sb & TypeOfLet a sb & TypeOfUniverse a sb & SameIsAlpha a sb
  & SameSeparates a sb & RefinesItself a sb & SubtypeRefinesBase a sb & RefinesFunctions a sb & RefinesSeparates a sb
  & BranchRefines a sb

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §5 The rules that read types

-- the elaborated acts of a name, and every application in a term with the context it sits in
declaredType (ep : Program) (n : String) : Maybe Term := match ep { nil -> nothing ;
  cons act rest -> match act { Declare x ty -> if x == n then just ty else declaredType rest n ; _ -> declaredType rest n } }
definedBody (ep : Program) (n : String) : Maybe Term := match ep { nil -> nothing ;
  cons act rest -> match act { Define x ty b -> if x == n then just b else definedBody rest n ; _ -> definedBody rest n } }
Application = { context : Context, function : Term, argument : Term }
applications (ctx : Context) (u : Term) : List Application := match u {
  App f x -> cons { context := ctx, function := f, argument := x } (appendApps (applications ctx f) (applications ctx x)) ;
  Lam x ty b -> appendApps (applications ctx ty) (applications (cons (x, ty) ctx) b) ;
  Pi x ty b -> appendApps (applications ctx ty) (applications (cons (x, ty) ctx) b) ;
  Sigma x ty b -> appendApps (applications ctx ty) (applications (cons (x, ty) ctx) b) ;
  Subtype x ty b -> appendApps (applications ctx ty) (applications (cons (x, ty) ctx) b) ;
  Let x ty v b -> appendApps (applications ctx ty) (appendApps (applications ctx v) (applications (cons (x, ty) ctx) b)) ;
  Pair x y -> appendApps (applications ctx x) (applications ctx y) ;
  Inj l x -> applications ctx x ;
  Match s arms -> appendApps (applications ctx s) (armsApplications ctx arms) ;
  _ -> nil ;
}
armsApplications (ctx : Context) (arms : List (Pattern * Term)) : List Application :=
  match arms { nil -> nil ; cons (q, b) rest -> appendApps (applications ctx b) (armsApplications ctx rest) }
appendApps (xs ys : List Application) : List Application := match xs { nil -> ys ; cons x rest -> cons x (appendApps rest ys) }
anyApp (f : Application -> Bool) (xs : List Application) : Bool := match xs { nil -> false ; cons x rest -> f x or anyApp f rest }
bodyApplications (a : Alpha) (e : Elaboration a) (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : List Application :=
  match definedBody (e.elaborate p) n { nothing -> nil ; just b -> applications nil b }

-- 4.R6: the body of a declared name has its type `T`, or `T -> Bool`, `T -> Failures E`, `Law T`,
-- compared under the theory's own parameters: for `T (a : A) : { ... }` and `T (a : A) := L a`,
-- the parameters are peeled from both before comparing (review of layers 0-1, B); a law may take
-- further quantified parameters after the model, `T -> X -> Bool`
fitsAt (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ty bt : Term) : Bool :=
  t.same bt ty or endsIn a sb t ty bt
endsIn (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ty bt : Term) : Bool := match bt {
  Pi x d c -> t.same d ty and verdictType c ; App f arg -> t.same bt (App (Var "Law") ty) ; _ -> false }
verdictType (c : Term) : Bool := match c {
  Var v -> v == "Bool" ; App f arg -> f == Var "Failures" ; Pi x d r -> verdictType r ; _ -> false }
fits (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ty : Term) (r : Maybe Term) : Bool := match r {
  nothing -> false ;
  just bt -> match ty { Pi x d c -> (match bt { Pi y e f -> t.same d e and fits a sb t c (just f) ; _ -> fitsAt a sb t ty bt }) ;
                        _ -> fitsAt a sb t ty bt } }
violatesR6 (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  isDeclared p n and isDefined p n and (match declaredType (e.elaborate p) n { nothing -> false ;
    just ty -> match definedBody (e.elaborate p) n { nothing -> false ;
      just b -> not (fits a sb t ty (t.typeOf (e.elaborate p) nil b)) } })

-- 4.R8: `==` only where equality is structural: never on a type that contains an exponential,
-- looked through the program's definitions of type names (fuel: the number of acts, so a
-- recursive `data` is looked through once)
-- (a `data`'s constructors are arrows into it: what is read is their argument types; a name is
-- looked through its definition, or its declaration when it is a theory declared by its record;
-- review of layers 0-1, B)
containsArrow (ep : Program) (fuel : Nat) (ty : Term) : Bool := match ty {
  Pi x d c -> true ;
  Sigma x d c -> containsArrow ep fuel d or containsArrow ep fuel c ;
  Subtype x d q -> containsArrow ep fuel d ;
  Sum kvs -> anyArrow ep fuel kvs ; Data x kvs -> anyArgumentArrow ep fuel kvs ; Record kvs -> anyArrow ep fuel kvs ;
  App f x -> containsArrow ep fuel f or containsArrow ep fuel x ;
  Var x -> fuel > 0 and (match definedBody ep x {
    just b -> containsArrow ep (fuel - 1) b ;
    nothing -> match declaredType ep x { just (Record kvs) -> anyArrow ep (fuel - 1) kvs ; _ -> false } }) ;
  _ -> false ;
}
arguments (ty : Term) : List Term := match ty { Pi x d c -> cons d (arguments c) ; _ -> nil }
anyArgumentArrow (ep : Program) (fuel : Nat) (kvs : List (String * Term)) : Bool := match kvs { nil -> false ;
  cons (k, v) rest -> anyTermArrow ep fuel (arguments v) or anyArgumentArrow ep fuel rest }
anyTermArrow (ep : Program) (fuel : Nat) (ts : List Term) : Bool :=
  match ts { nil -> false ; cons u rest -> containsArrow ep fuel u or anyTermArrow ep fuel rest }
anyArrow (ep : Program) (fuel : Nat) (kvs : List (String * Term)) : Bool :=
  match kvs { nil -> false ; cons (k, v) rest -> containsArrow ep fuel v or anyArrow ep fuel rest }
actCount (ep : Program) : Nat := match ep { nil -> 0 ; cons act rest -> 1 + actCount rest }
eqOnArrow (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ep : Program) (ap : Application) : Bool :=
  match ap.function { App f x -> f == Var "==" and (match t.typeOf ep ap.context x { nothing -> false ;
    just ty -> containsArrow ep (actCount ep) ty }) ; _ -> false }
violatesR8 (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  anyApp (fn ap { eqOnArrow a sb t (e.elaborate p) ap }) (bodyApplications a e p n)

-- 4.R9: an argument passes where its function's domain is expected only if its base refines the
-- domain's base; a refinement the argument does not carry is an obligation (4.R5, 4.R11), not a
-- failure (review of layers 0-1, B)
base (ty : Term) : Term := match ty { Subtype x d q -> base d ; _ -> ty }
mismatch (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (t : Typing a sb) (ep : Program) (ap : Application) : Bool :=
  match t.typeOf ep ap.context ap.function { nothing -> false ;
    just ft -> match ft { Pi x d c -> (match t.typeOf ep ap.context ap.argument { nothing -> false ;
                                          just at -> not (t.refines (base at) (base d)) }) ;
                          _ -> false } }
violatesR9 (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  anyApp (fn ap { mismatch a sb t (e.elaborate p) ap }) (bodyApplications a e p n)

-- 4.R11 is a law of the typing (`BranchRefines`): a checker that types branches by it rejects no
-- program the rule accepts. 4.R13 (an operator resolved by the type, one meaning per types) and
-- 4.S23 (implicit arguments from the expected type) are laws of the elaboration (step 2.4).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §6 Reports

-- What does not reject is reported (4.S19, 4.S20): a provisional extern (4.R5), a loose function
-- (4.S17: a top-level definition at a bare exponential, until local definitions exist), and a
-- `data` whose constructors no law mentions (4.R3, reported besides). Whether a law characterizes
-- or only compares (4.R10, 4.S20) is the author's judgement, reported by name only.
reportedAs (rs : List Report) (kind n : String) : Bool :=
  match rs { nil -> false ; cons r rest -> (r.kind == kind and r.name == n) or reportedAs rest kind n }
provisionalExtern (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  anyAct (fn act { match act { define x bs t b -> (match b { termBody u -> isExtern u and isProvisional u ; _ -> false }) ;
                              _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)
looseFunction (p : SurfaceProgram) (n : String) : Bool :=
  anyAct (fn act { match act { define x bs t b -> nonEmptyBinders bs or (match t { just (binop o l r) -> o == "->" ; _ -> false }) ;
                              _ -> false } }) (actsNamed p n)
nonEmptyBinders (bs : List Binder) : Bool := match bs { nil -> false ; cons b rest -> true }
ReportsWhen (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (kind : String)
            (holds : SurfaceProgram -> String -> Bool) (w : WellFormed a sb e t) (c : Violating holds) : Bool :=
  reportedAs (w.report c.p) kind c.n
ReportsOnlyWhen (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) (kind : String)
                (holds : SurfaceProgram -> String -> Bool) (w : WellFormed a sb e t) (c : Clean holds) : Bool :=
  not (reportedAs (w.report c.p) kind c.n)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §7 WellFormed

-- A checker reports every failure of each rule, and no failure where a complete predicate finds
-- none (4.R1, 4.R4, 4.R5, 4.R7); the predicates still partial have the first law only. It reports
-- only about the program's names, and reports what does not reject, an unclaimed law (4.S14)
-- among it.
WellFormed (a : Alpha) (sb : Substitution a) (e : Elaboration a) (t : Typing a sb) :=
  ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R1" violatesR1 & ReportsNoFalseFailure a sb e t "4.R1" violatesR1
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R2" violatesR2Exists & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R3" violatesR3
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R4" violatesR4 & ReportsNoFalseFailure a sb e t "4.R4" violatesR4
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R5" violatesR5 & ReportsNoFalseFailure a sb e t "4.R5" violatesR5
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R6" (violatesR6 a sb e t)
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R7" violatesR7 & ReportsNoFalseFailure a sb e t "4.R7" violatesR7
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R8" (violatesR8 a sb e t) & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R9" (violatesR9 a sb e t)
  & ReportsViolations a sb e t "4.R12" violatesR12 & ReportsOnItsNames a sb e t
  & ReportsWhen a sb e t "unclaimed" violatesS14 & ReportsOnlyWhen a sb e t "unclaimed" violatesS14
  & ReportsWhen a sb e t "provisional" provisionalExtern & ReportsOnlyWhen a sb e t "provisional" provisionalExtern
  & ReportsWhen a sb e t "loose" looseFunction & ReportsOnlyWhen a sb e t "loose" looseFunction
